            {
                "entry_id": "6d15d19a-2b62-3114-9302-d1fe19146b70",
                "word": "billy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a0e3e6d1-8b6a-434c-85a3-fbc1e06ea93c",
                        "entry_id": "6d15d19a-2b62-3114-9302-d1fe19146b70",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "billies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "862fc702-43d2-3dcd-aee6-3db9554d4ae8",
                        "entry_id": "6d15d19a-2b62-3114-9302-d1fe19146b70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A highwayman's club, billy club."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7acf05ef-b2bd-3901-973d-3b8820ad18fe",
                        "entry_id": "6d15d19a-2b62-3114-9302-d1fe19146b70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A slubbing or roving machine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f60376d-b955-4e69-801e-37caa7c68c65",
                                "sense_id": "7acf05ef-b2bd-3901-973d-3b8820ad18fe",
                                "text": "[…]at the time there existed in Dublin and its immediate neighbourhood, “forty-five manufacturers, having twenty-two billies, giving employment to 2885 work people, on whom depended for support 7386 individuals, manufacturing 29,312 pieces of cloth, of various qualities, valued at £336,380.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98e97c2e-ffa5-436b-b86d-0681bafe7847",
                                "sense_id": "7acf05ef-b2bd-3901-973d-3b8820ad18fe",
                                "text": "On the second floor there were 2 billies, 1 carding and 1 scribbling machine."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fbc3cd21-358c-3aef-9580-d49d5273db7d",
                        "entry_id": "6d15d19a-2b62-3114-9302-d1fe19146b70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tin with a swing handle used to boil tea over an open fire; a billycan; a billypot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10f132ab-d172-43aa-8e38-bb3e54dbb19c",
                                "sense_id": "fbc3cd21-358c-3aef-9580-d49d5273db7d",
                                "text": "Let's get the billy and cook some beans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "821e8ad7-ae11-446c-92d9-5e390a729636",
                                "sense_id": "fbc3cd21-358c-3aef-9580-d49d5273db7d",
                                "text": "We had been absent from civilisation, so long, that our tin billies, the only boiling utensils we had, got completely worn or burnt out at the bottoms, and as the boilings for glue and oil must still go on, what were we to do with billies with no bottoms?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1132f2b-549a-402c-ba68-906879028ae0",
                                "sense_id": "fbc3cd21-358c-3aef-9580-d49d5273db7d",
                                "text": "Oh there once was a swagman camped in the billabong,\nUnder the shade of a coolibah tree,\nAnd he sang as he looked at the old billy boiling,\n'Who'll come a'waltzing Matilda, with me.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d11d89eb-f0c5-4bda-9a01-1cf07c431cef",
                                "sense_id": "fbc3cd21-358c-3aef-9580-d49d5273db7d",
                                "text": "Mother prepared a splendid picnic. […] Rugs, food and the black billy for making tea, were packed into the old baby buggy and we trundled it straight down Simcoe Street."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c6969e9-3b0c-46fa-9e42-035fc40da824",
                                "sense_id": "fbc3cd21-358c-3aef-9580-d49d5273db7d",
                                "text": "Over the fence, in a shallow gully 100 metres away, this guy and his wife were living on the dirt in the open weather with just a blanket, billies, a dog and a transistor radio. They didn't even have water."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "82e70b12-731d-3a1e-83a6-c38e2b53dcdc",
                        "entry_id": "6d15d19a-2b62-3114-9302-d1fe19146b70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A bong for smoking marijuana."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d569cc07-f8fd-3503-b6a8-6a8e7d16dac0",
                        "entry_id": "6d15d19a-2b62-3114-9302-d1fe19146b70",
