            {
                "entry_id": "48cda776-abc5-3f5c-9e7d-3b69f56210c3",
                "word": "billy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8caac88e-92e9-46ee-8774-0627708e9adf",
                        "entry_id": "48cda776-abc5-3f5c-9e7d-3b69f56210c3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "billies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5289c254-d004-3254-841f-f6076d5fb13e",
                        "entry_id": "48cda776-abc5-3f5c-9e7d-3b69f56210c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fellow, companion, comrade, mate; partner, brother."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df97faa9-ef57-3308-8f8a-7e80a4890950",
                        "entry_id": "48cda776-abc5-3f5c-9e7d-3b69f56210c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A good friend."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Geordie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7134cead-cbec-4b76-b405-da3108067797",
                                "sense_id": "df97faa9-ef57-3308-8f8a-7e80a4890950",
                                "text": "Fareweel, my rhyme-compoſing billie! / Your native ſoil was right ill-willie; / But may ye flouriſh like a lily, / Now bonilie! / I'll toaſt ye in my hindmoſt gillie, / Tho' owre the Sea!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5136b7cc-fcea-3c5c-882a-3ff8f6e16fc5",
                        "entry_id": "48cda776-abc5-3f5c-9e7d-3b69f56210c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A billy goat."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "25937cdd-651c-42c7-8c35-0026d513cfd4",
                                "sense_id": "5136b7cc-fcea-3c5c-882a-3ff8f6e16fc5",
                                "text": "1970 August, Valerius Geist, Mountain Goat Mysteries, Field & Stream, page 62,\nThen, during three days, I was amazed to see nannies with kids attack and chase off large billies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d2ced2b-645d-422f-9744-f861b029dab5",
                                "sense_id": "5136b7cc-fcea-3c5c-882a-3ff8f6e16fc5",
                                "text": "In fact, distinguishing between billies and nannies isn't necessarily a sure thing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f03301bb-d5f8-494b-9f39-37e8249ddd23",
                                "sense_id": "5136b7cc-fcea-3c5c-882a-3ff8f6e16fc5",
                                "text": "It isn't just billies that enter the bleak season with rut-depleted fat reserves, but rams, bull elk, buck deer, and others."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "784c9a88-f055-3358-a556-ce961127a8b3",
                        "entry_id": "48cda776-abc5-3f5c-9e7d-3b69f56210c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A silk handkerchief."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "obsolete",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d487507-caf1-44e9-bfff-0d15c7823875",
                                "sense_id": "784c9a88-f055-3358-a556-ce961127a8b3",
                                "text": "All fighting coves you too must know, / Ben Caunt as well as Bendigo, / And to each mill be sure to go, / […] And you must sport a blue billy, / Or a yellow wipe […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
